A||||3||Wannabe||Which years for t-tops?||||1||
Z||000000||Wannabe||03-11-2001||10:23 AM||||There is an add in the local paper for an '86  V6 Fiero with t-tops. I was under the impression that '88 was the only year for t-tops and that there were no aftermarket kits. In other words, the car for sale may actually be an '88. Any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Mi Junk||03-11-2001||10:33 AM||||88 was the only year for factory installed. C+C did the mod, but you could get it done on any year of car by them.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/85_sig_2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Tina||03-11-2001||01:32 PM||||I've you decide against getting it, <BR>let me know.<BR>Still looking for a T-Top.<P>Tina<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||03-11-2001||03:15 PM||||Mi Junk is correct......any year Fiero can have T-Tops.  C&C actually started making kits for them back in '85 and it took a few years to convince GM that it was a viable option (and was safe) for them to include on their option list.<P>GM finally gave the go ahead for a T-Top option in '88.  It was to have an official RPO code (CJB) and could be ordered from the dealer.  The Fieros were built then shipped to C&C's factory for the conversion.  This is why the '88 T-Top cars are referred to as "ship thru's".......all others are referred to as "kits".  <P>It should be noted that all T-Tops are the same, whether a kit or ship thru.  The only differences are cosmetic.......the trim caps on ship thrus are molded in the proper color while the kits (at least the ones I have seen) are all pinted to match the interior.  Also, the seals are different.....the ship thrus have a built in lip to cover the headliner (where it meets the seal) while the kits have a separate rubber strip to do the job.  <P>I've owned several T-Top Fieros......an '85 SE & '88 Formula.......both "kits", and an '88 Formula and '88 GT.......both "ship thrus".  All were about the same, as far as fit and finish are concerned.  Actually, my '85 SE (converted in '89) was a much better install than any of the facory installs I've owned.  It never leaked, creaked or squeaked!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>At any rate...if that '86 is everything you want in a Fiero  AND it has T-Tops then go for it.  T-Tops are a blast in the spring/summer.  ||||reg||1
